# fixedbugs, M-reflection-verdict, 2026-09-12 (defect 027).
#
# SYMPTOM: a binding the compiler had **deliberately widened to admit** could
# be declared and not built. `heroes build` died with
#
#     internal error: compiling the generated C failed:
#     main.hero:6:37: error: initializing 'char *' with an expression of type
#     'const char *' discards qualifiers
#     [-Werror,-Wincompatible-pointer-types-discards-qualifiers]
#
# at exit 2 — a message that accuses the compiler's own internals and names no
# repair, for a program `spec § 13` says should either work or be refused by a
# diagnostic about the header.
#
# CAUSE, and it is the part worth reading: **the rule was already settled and
# the construction did not follow it.** `cstr` emits `const char *`, and a
# header's member is often plain `char *` — `struct passwd`'s `pw_name`,
# `pw_dir` and `pw_shell` are named in `selfhost/emit/extern_field.hero`'s own
# comment, because panel 089 widened the per-field `_Static_assert` to accept
# both spellings and wrote down why: *"const on the pointee restricts WRITES,
# and the language offers none through a `cstr`"*. So the DECLARATION was
# legal, the assertion passed, and then the compound literal
# `(struct passwd){.pw_name = t2}` was refused by this project's own
# `-Werror=incompatible-pointer-types-discards-qualifiers`.
#
# FIX: `selfhost/emit/aggregate.hero::written_as` casts a `cstr` value to
# `__typeof__` of the member, for foreign records only and `cstr` fields only —
# the same form the assertion above it already uses to ask about that member,
# so the value is written as exactly the type the header gives and nothing new
# is asserted about what that type is. Everywhere else the compound literal's
# own type checking is what catches a wrong argument, and it keeps it.
#
# **WHAT GUARDS THIS, said plainly rather than implied.** No suite clangs a
# `fixedbugs/` case: this directory gets `annotations`, `canonical` and
# `emission`, and `--emit-c` never calls clang. So what this file guards is the
# EMISSION — the cast is in the blessed C and a regression would move it — and
# the proof that the program builds is a run recorded in the commit that
# repaired it: `heroes build` at exit 0 on this Mac, against exit 2 before.
# A case that looked like a compile guard and was not would be worse than none.

extern "pwd.h"
    record Passwd tag passwd partial
        pw_name: cstr
        pw_dir: cstr

function main()
    # All three shapes: a null field, a lent string, and a record with two
    # non-const members rather than one, since the repair is per field.
    empty = Passwd(pw_name: nullptr, pw_dir: nullptr)
    print(empty.pw_name == nullptr)
    here = "/tmp"
    filled = Passwd(pw_name: nullptr, pw_dir: here.cstr())
    print(filled.pw_dir == nullptr)
